[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; The checkpoint's soul sink. Inherits ModalPanel.tscn and adds four stat rows and a close button.
; Replaces GameplayHud.CreateLevelUpPanel.
;
; THE FOUR ROWS ARE AUTHORED, NOT A LIST. There are four PlayerStat values and there always will be,
; so this is not the gate list's problem: the rows exist here, in PlayerStat's declaration order
; (Vitality, Endurance, Strength, Resolve), and RefreshLevelUp only writes their text and their
; disabled flag. The names LevelUpVitalityButton..LevelUpResolveButton are what the script's
; $"LevelUp{stat}Button" lookup expects.
;
; A row is wider and smaller-lettered than a menu button - 520 rather than 280, 20pt rather than the
; theme's 24 - because it carries four columns of text (stat, level, what a level gives, price)
; where 계속하기 carries one word. Both are overrides on top of MenuTheme, which still supplies the
; five state plates and the disabled text colour that make an unaffordable row readable as such.
;
; Subtitle is the karma line - what CreateLevelUpPanel called LevelUpSouls - and keeps the base's
; Cold200 and 24pt, because a resource count is exactly what that colour is for.
;
; This panel does not stop the world, which is why GameplayHud.tscn puts it under the pause panel in
; tree order: Escape has to be able to open the pause menu on top of it.
;
; UNITS: screen pixels.

